   "body": "Operator decision 2026-10-28 (UX), for this lot and its PR #292:\n\n- **(A) Text size and density.** A text-size slider is required, with a range below the current default, and a dense display (compact rows). PR #292's slider (`text_size_percent`, 70–130 %, step 5, offset on Dynamic Type) and `compact_mode` match the decision: keep them. Applying them to every screen (lists, sidebar, settings, reader) is the new lot **LOT-169 (#295)**, priority high.\n- **(B) Navigation.** The legacy bottom bar \"Catégories / Favoris / Messages / Plus\" stays. The intentional difference \"no tab bar in the split view\" (dropped `tabbar_minimize_on_scroll`, `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` #19 in #292) is reversed by the new lot **LOT-170 (#296)**, which restores the tabs, moves the settings entry into Plus and brings the row back. No need to block #292 on it: the start-screen setting keeps its legacy values (`tab:categories|favorites|messages`), so LOT-170 maps them to tabs again.\n\nAcceptance criteria added here:\n- [ ] The slider's lower bound stays below 100 % (smaller than the default), and the value is stored as an offset on Dynamic Type.\n- [ ] The spec and the CHANGELOG-LEGACY entry say the tab-bar removal is temporary until LOT-170 (#296), not a decision.\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
