   "body": "Community evidence and the settings diet (HFR+ topic, community, 2026-10-28; beta topic p. 1 #31–#37, #21–#24): the legacy maintainer says there are \"far too many settings, people don't know they exist\"; members agree but ask not to remove everything; members did not know the Favoris-mode setting existed. List titles bigger than post text split opinions; one global scale was added (matches LOT-169 (#295)).\n\nAcceptance criteria added here:\n- [ ] The spec's settings inventory marks each legacy setting keep / merge / drop, with the reason; key settings (Favoris mode, image loading) are also reachable in context on their screen.\n- [ ] The inventory is reconciled with the list of settings to drop or merge that the storage ADR draft (in progress) will produce; whichever lands second aligns with the first.\n",
